# | # ext2split1108.sh -- issue 1108: writes into holes under full extent nodes, and appends that grow
# | # the tree, on files whose extent trees Linux filled.
# | #
# | #   ext2split1108.sh seed  <volume-id>     on Linux: partition and seed the data volume
# | #   ext2split1108.sh haiku [step...]       on Haiku, with the data volume attached
# | #   ext2split1108.sh check <volume-id>     on Linux, afterwards: e2fsck -fn, the tree shapes, and
# | #                                          the contents (each written range, and the rest unchanged)
# | #
# | # The volume: one 2 GiB EBS volume, GPT, three ext4 file systems made by Ubuntu mke2fs, without
# | # journal or orphan_file (as in #1105's seed). Linux appends extents in logical order, so ext4
# | # splits each full leaf at its end and every node but the last on each level stays full.
# | #  p1 x4k  4 KiB blocks (340 entries per node), no metadata_csum:
# | #     fa   2000 written 1-block extents at even blocks, size 4000 blocks: depth 2, 5 full leaves
# | #     fu   the same with preallocated (unwritten) extents. A hole next to one can't merge into it,
# | #          so every fill there needs a new extent.
# | #     gh   1360 unwritten extents at even blocks: depth 1, the root and all 4 leaves full
# | #     gd   the same, size = the end of the last extent: an append must grow the tree
# | #     gk   the same at odd blocks (a leading hole): the grown root's key must be 1, not 0
# | #     tf4  4 written 64 KiB extents: a full root in the inode
# | #  p2 x1k  1 KiB blocks (84 entries per node), no metadata_csum:
# | #     kd   28224 unwritten extents at even blocks: depth 2, every node full (4 x 84 x 84), so one
# | #          new extent splits a leaf and an index node, and grows the root to depth 3
# | #     ku   3000 unwritten extents at even blocks: depth 2; 1 MiB written over 512 holes
# | #  p3 c4k  4 KiB blocks, metadata_csum:
# | #     cu   1360 unwritten extents at even blocks: depth 1, root and leaves full
# | #     cw   700 written extents at even blocks: depth 1, 2 full leaves
# | #  p4 e4k  ext2, 4 KiB blocks, indirect-mapped (regression: the goal change reaches DataStream):
# | #     ix   truncate -s 40M, 4 KiB at 0 and at 39 MiB (holes with missing indirect blocks)
# | #     iy   8 MiB of data, for an append
# | #  p5 fx   ext4, 4 KiB blocks, 48 MiB (regression: ENOSPC):
# | #     fz   700 written extents at even blocks; Haiku fills the volume, then writes into fz's holes
# | #
# | # Haiku steps (each one mounts, writes, syncs and unmounts):
# | #   fa / fu: 8 KiB at block 1 (first leaf), 8 KiB at block 1001 (third leaf), 1 MiB at block 2001
# | #   gh: 8 KiB at block 681 (second leaf)
# | #   gd / gk: append 64 KiB
# | #   tf4: 64 KiB at 1 MiB (between the root's extents)
# | #   kd: 8 KiB at 1 KiB-block 20000;  ku: 1 MiB at 2 MiB
# | #   cu: 64 KiB at block 681, 8 KiB at block 1101;  cw: 64 KiB at block 341
# | #   ix: 64 KiB at 32 KiB and at 20 MiB (indirect holes); iy: append 64 KiB
# | #   nospc: fill fx, write into fz's holes (ENOSPC expected), remove the filler
